SUBENT        C1451001   20260728   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                  5         10
TITLE      The influence of low-energy resonances on the
           reaction rate of 18O(alpha,gamma)22Ne
AUTHOR     (U.Giesen,C.P.Browne,J.Gorres,J.G.Ross,M.Wiescher,
           R.E.Azuma,J.D.King,J.B.Vise,M.Buckby)
REFERENCE  (J,NP/A,567,146,1994)
           #doi:10.1016/0375-9474(94)90731-5
INSTITUTE  (1USANOT,1CANTOR)
HISTORY    (20060724C) DR
           (20260728A) BP: Updated entry, added second experiment
                      and resonance parameters.
ENDBIB              10
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           13
SUBENT        C1451002   20260728   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                  8         22
REACTION   (8-O-18(3-LI-6,EL)8-O-18,,DA,,RTH)
FACILITY   (VDGT,1USANOT) The FN-tandem accelerator at the
           Nuclear Structure Laboratory of the University of
           Notre Dame.
INC-SOURCE A 6Li beam energy of 32 MeV to assure a predominantly
           direct reaction mechanism. 7Li beam energy of 16 MeV.
           The typical Li beam intensity varied between 100 and
           500 Na on target.
DETECTOR   (MAGSP,PROPC,SCIN) A 100 cm broad-range magnetic
           spectrograph and detected at the focal plane with a
           position-sensitive proportional counter system backed
           by a scintillator to measure position, energy loss
           and total energy of the incoming reaction products.
SAMPLE     The 180 targets were prepared by evaporating an
           approximately 50 microg/cm2 thick layer of W18O onto
           a 380 microg/cm2 gold foil. The thickness of the W18O
           layer was determined and possible target contaminants
           were identified from the elastic scattering of 6Li at
           an energy of 32 MeV.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No information on uncertainties.
STATUS     (CURVE,,U.Giesen+,J,NP/A,567,146,1994) Fig. - 5
HISTORY    (20260728A) BP: Updated STATUS, corrected spelling.
ENDBIB              22
